---
source: crates/instrukt-cli/tests/harness.rs
expression: help
---
The sessions facade over the configured runtime

Usage: instrukt sessions <COMMAND>

Commands:
  run            Start a session through the runtime mapping; prints its id
  send           Send text to a session; prints its id
  alive          Print a session's status: running, needs-input, ended ok, ended failed or gone
  conversation   Print a session's conversation
  link           Link two sessions of one runtime, or remove their link
  end            End a session, your own (`self`), or a todo's bound sessions (`--todo`); says so
                 when the runtime needs no ending
  history        Look up earlier conversations in the runtime you are running in
  resolve-start  Resolve a standing agent's start whose result never arrived: bind the session the
                 runtime did create, or declare that none was
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Exit status 3, "yours to do": the runtime fills this call as an instruction for you. instrukt ran
nothing; it printed the instruction (with the call's inputs after it, one per line). Carry it out
with your own runtime's tools; that completes the call. It is neither success nor failure.
